#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:1
msgid "Formats live outside the engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:3
msgid ""
"*Implemented.* The project's main structural bet, and the reason there is"
" an engine at all rather than a program per issuer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:6
msgid "The bet: the engine knows no report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:7
msgid ""
"The engine knows **nothing** about any particular report. What it knows "
"is how to run a schedule of steps over classified pages, feed each page "
"through pipelines, and resolve what comes out. Which pages, and what to "
"do with them, comes from a **formats repository** — an ordinary "
"directory, in its own version control, maintained by whoever cares about "
"those reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:12
msgid ""
"The consequence is the point: **supporting a new report needs no release "
"of the engine**, touches nothing anyone else maintains, and can be "
"published independently. `analysis_finance_reports_formats` is one such "
"repository, and there is nothing privileged about it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:16
msgid "What keeping formats outside buys, and what it costs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:17
msgid ""
"**Buys:** the part that does not change and the part that grows "
"constantly are versioned, tested and released separately. A layout that "
"breaks costs one repository a fix, not a release of everything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:20
msgid ""
"**Costs:** the engine cannot validate a format against a report it has "
"never seen, so a misconfigured repository fails at run time rather than "
"at build time. This is why so much of the engine's error handling is "
"about **naming the row, the file and the format** — those errors are the "
"only feedback a repository author gets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:25
msgid ""
"It is also why an unknown key, an unknown column and a page class no step"
" mentions are all **errors** rather than things ignored. In a plugin "
"system, silence is the enemy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:28
msgid "Three levels of effort, merged by name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:30
msgid ""
"A format can be specified at three levels, differing in how much of the "
"algorithm the author supplies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "The algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "Its parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "You write"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "**structured**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "in the library, fixed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "columns of a CSV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "rows in a spreadsheet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "**semistructured**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "in the library *by name*, or your own module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "YAML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "a name and a configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "**unstructured**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "in the repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "in the code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:39
msgid ""
"They **add up** rather than exclude one another. Merging happens by "
"summing the **same-named** pipelines of the three levels, and that is the"
" **only** place the three levels meet: no other part of the engine knows "
"they exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:43
msgid "Why the merge is the interesting part"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:45
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Because irregularity is rarely uniform. A report whose investment table "
"is perfectly ordinary may still name its funds in a way nothing can "
"parameterise. Being able to inherit two segments and write the third is "
"what keeps a hard format from costing three times a simple one — and it "
"only works because the segments are separable ({doc}`segments`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:50
msgid ""
"The design would fail if the levels were **alternatives**: an author "
"hitting one irregular detail would have to drop to Python for the whole "
"format, and the structured level would serve only the formats that need "
"nothing at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:54
msgid "Collisions are errors, not precedence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:56
msgid ""
"Defining the same semistructured algorithm name **both** natively and in "
"your own module is an error rather than a precedence rule to be "
"remembered. The check runs over every native name of the segment as soon "
"as your module loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/formats-as-plugins.md:60
msgid ""
"A collision is nearly always a typo, and letting one side win silently is"
" what makes a typo expensive. The same reasoning as unknown keys, applied"
" to names."
msgstr ""

